    "President Donald Trump claimed he spoke with a former president who expressed regret regarding not attacking Iran when they occupied the Oval Office.",
    "Representatives for each of the four living former presidents—three Democrats and one Republican—said none have been in contact with Trump recently since his inauguration on January 20, 2025.",
    "The text notes that President Trump declined to name the specific former president when asked by reporters."
  ],
  "biasSummary": "The article presents conflicting reports between Trump's allegations and the denials provided by current White House representatives, potentially indicating editorial bias in how past political relationships are reported."
}

{
    "description": "Jane Fonda makes a light‑hearted jab at Barbra Streisand for receiving an Oscar tribute to late co‑star Robert Redford, claiming she made four films together while Streisand only one, and urges her to deliver her own tribute.",
    "articleSummary": "During the 98th Academy Awards’ In Memoriam segment, Barbra Streisand performed an emotional tributes to Robert Redford, playing a section of “The Way We Were,” celebrating his legacy, independence and iconic collaborations. Jane Fonda, who starred in four films with Redford, is publicly amused by the spotlight given to Streisand, asserting she made more movies together and that Redford was a “thoughtful and bold” intellectual cowboy who protected press freedom and revitalized indie cinema.",
    "points": [
        "Jane Fonda said, “She only made one movie with him; I made four! I have more to say.”",
        "Jane Fonda called Redford “thoughtful and bold,” praised his activism, and said she made four films together.",
        "Streisand delivered an Oscar In Memoriam tribute that included a section of “The Way We Were” and a comment that she and Redford were such opposites but found out more about each other."
    ],
    "biasSummary": "The article mainly reports Fonda’s playful remark questioning Streisand’s absence from her own tribute, which gives Fonda’s perspective more prominence. The tone celebrates Redford’s achievements without overt political agenda, but the focus on Fonda’s criticism reflects a slight bias toward her view."
}
